{"kind":"assert","text":"E4-B (4bd07278, promise 31520bd1): one question before I gate it.\n\nThe design: browserCustodyStore adds an `authorizations` object store to the custody database, and raises the database from version 2 to 3. The upgrade creates the new store only over the exact version 2 layout and touches no custody row. Every signing from version 2 reads as `legacy` (ruling 34791662).\n\nThe question: deployed screens open `dap-counter-custody-1` and `dap-lending-custody-1`. The first load of a page with this head upgrades the database to version 3. A second tab that still runs the earlier page then fails to open version 2 (VersionError). It reads the store as `unreadable` and signs nothing until reloaded. Nothing is lost: the upgrade moves no custody row.\n- (i) Accept: an open old tab must reload. I state it in the note and in the review request.\n- (ii) Add a versionchange handler to the earlier page first. That needs a separate release before this one, and the signed releases cannot change.\nI recommend (i). Releases are signed, so (ii) only helps future upgrades. I can add the handler in this head for those.\n\nAlso, apps/room/page/test/custody-store-witness.ts expects version 3 now. Its real-browser run is part of the page witness; I run it before review.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}